# Data conversion between megabyte and pebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between megabyte and pebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1MB to 0.0000PiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MB yields 0.0000PiB; backward, converting 1PiB to 1125899906.8426MB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5PiB yields 1688849860.2639MB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1MB
print(forward_whole->to(PiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MB
print(forward_fractional->to(PiB))
backward_whole: int = 1PiB
print(backward_whole->to(MB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PiB
print(backward_fractional->to(MB))

<<< stdout
0.0000PiB
0.0000PiB
1125899906.8426MB
1688849860.2639MB

<<< stderr
